# media-hub — code and contracts are versioned; data and secrets are not.
#
# This repo is the SYSTEM, not the library. media.db is the canonical
# store (ARCHITECTURE.md) and stays local: it is a 49MB binary holding a
# personal viewing history, it changes on every run, and it is under a
# one-writer-at-a-time rule that git would happily violate. Everything
# derived from it is likewise local — it can always be rebuilt from the
# DB by the loaders in this repo.

# --- secrets -------------------------------------------------------------
# sync-config.json carries live Plex / Ryot / TMDB tokens in plaintext.
sync-config.json
*.env
.env
**/sources.env
*_token.json
.mcp.json
# ...but the empty templates are the whole point — they document the shape.
!*.example.env
!sync-config.example.json

# --- the canonical store and its backups ---------------------------------
media.db
media.db-wal
media.db-shm
media.db.bak
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
backups/

# --- raw-first snapshots (immutable local archives, regenerable) ---------
sources/
recommend/raw/
**/_archive-*/

# --- derived / generated artifacts ---------------------------------------
# All rebuildable: library.html by build_library_db.py, out/ by render.py,
# covers by fetch_covers_db.py and render.py.
library.html
review.html
covers/
recommend/covers/
recommend/out/
exports/
dumps/

# --- personal data dumps --------------------------------------------------
# analysis/ keeps its markdown and its decision records; the bulk dumps of
# review text and mined ratings are media.db data by another name.
analysis/reviews_dump_*.txt
analysis/taste_mining_*.json

# Letterboxd CSVs are the sole surviving copy of a deleted account
# (CLAUDE.md) — irreplaceable data, not code. Back them up deliberately,
# not as a side effect of a code push.
letterboxd-import/

# --- archives -------------------------------------------------------------
attic/

# --- caches ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.superpowers/
.worktrees/
.DS_Store

# --- iCloud conflict copies ----------------------------------------------
# This folder lives in iCloud Documents, which silently creates
# "foo 2.py"-style duplicates (CLAUDE.md).
* [0-9].*
*\ [0-9].*
.icloud
